# Application configuration

`rocci.toml` configures the desktop host and packaging flow. The schema rejects
unknown fields so misspelled security or bundle settings cannot fail silently.

## Complete shape

```toml
[app]
name = "Datastar"
identifier = "dev.rocci.datastar"
version = "0.1.0"

[[windows]]
label = "main"
title = "Datastar"
url = "/"
width = 1040
height = 760
min_width = 720
min_height = 560
visible = true

[http]
host = "127.0.0.1"
port = 0
redirect_trailing_slash = true

[security]
allowed_origins = []

[assets]
directory = "assets"
embed = true
datastar = "1.0.2"

[development]
reload = false
devtools = false

[bundle]
app = "."
macos_plist = "macos/Info.plist"
```

## App

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `name` | User-visible application name |
| `identifier` | Reverse-domain bundle identifier |
| `version` | Optional application version |

The identifier must be safe for platform packaging.

## Windows

At least one `[[windows]]` entry is required. Labels must be unique. Dimensions
are logical pixels; minimum dimensions and visibility are optional.

## HTTP

`host` must be `127.0.0.1` or `localhost`. `port = 0` chooses an available
port. `redirect_trailing_slash = true` sends a 308 between `/page` and
`/page/` when the other form is registered.

## Security

`allowed_origins` accepts explicit HTTP origins. The default content security
policy is self-hosted and blocks objects, base URLs, and framing. It currently
allows `unsafe-eval` because Datastar evaluates declarative expressions.

Use a custom `csp` only when you understand every source the application needs.

## Assets

`directory` selects the asset tree and `embed` controls bundle embedding.
`datastar` is either an exact version string such as `"1.0.2"` or `false` when
the app supplies its own runtime.

## Development

`frontend_url` and `backend_url`, when set, must be loopback URLs. `reload` and
`devtools` control development behavior.

## Bundle

`app` points to the app source, `macos_plist` selects a plist, and repeated
`[[bundle.resources]]` records copy `from` paths to `to` destinations.

Validate the resolved file before running or bundling:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- validate rocci.toml
```
